  "goodToKnow": "Die Scherbe, usually plural Scherben, is a shard of broken glass or china: Scherben zusammenkehren. Scherben bringen Glück (broken pieces bring luck) is said to comfort people, and at the Polterabend before a wedding, guests smash crockery on purpose. But broken mirrors mean bad luck. Vor einem Scherbenhaufen stehen means to face the ruins of a relationship or project. Plural: die Scherben."
